  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I could not run `vite build` or open the app in a browser here, so the rendering and ball behaviour are untested. I also never confirmed how the engine positions 3D text or lays out the DOM overlay.\n\n- **Board:** it is 8 wide by 12 tall. It has a back panel, side walls, a faint transparent front pane, and 9 staggered rows of pegs alternating 7 and 6 (59 pegs) as one instanced mesh. Seven bins sit underneath with dividers and alternating back colours. Their numbers 1 to 7 are 3D text, and a live count for each bin is shown in a DOM overlay beneath them.\n- **Look:** pegs are silver metal, balls are gold, and bins are blue and purple. There is a key light, a blue rim light and a neutral environment. The perspective camera is framed so the whole board and the labels are visible.\n- **Physics:** I wrote my own 2D rigid-body simulation instead of using the engine's Rapier physics. The docs left Rapier's setup and startup unclear, and I wanted a result I could make repeatable. It runs at a fixed 1/240 s step with gravity, restitution 0.4, friction, and collisions against pegs, walls, dividers and other balls. One ball (index 4) gets a horizontal offset of exactly 0 and would otherwise balance on the centre peg, so I added a small deterministic nudge to break that tie.\n- **Spawning:** balls spawn at the top centre every 0.25 simulated seconds with offset `((i*37)%11-5)*0.02`.\n- **Buttons:** \"Drop 20 Balls\" starts a fresh batch and is ignored while a drop is running. \"Reset\" clears the balls and counts.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only getter, refreshed every frame, with `phase`, `spawned`, `bins` and `total`. The phase becomes `settled` once all 20 balls are in bins and nearly still for 0.5 simulated seconds. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n- **Bin counting:** a ball counts toward a bin as soon as it is below the divider height, even if it is still moving.\n\n",
